// Left shift past the top of `int128`.
//
// The usual carry-out test is `shifted & ~maskFor(bits)`, and at 128 bits
// `~maskFor(128)` is zero -- there is no 129th bit. Both the VM and the folder need
// the operand-vs-limit comparison instead, or the shift silently wraps.

function main():void {
    int128 maxv = 170141183460469231731687303715884105727i128;
    print("before\n");
    int128 doubled = maxv << 1;
    print(doubled);
    eof: pass;
}
